## 1. Purpose and intended use

Rank customers by calibrated churn probability to choose whom to contact in a retention campaign. Decision rule: contact customers whose probability is above p* = {{ "%.4f"|format(p_star) }}, up to the campaign capacity. Capacity is {{ campaign_capacity }} contacts per period from a population of {{ population_per_period }} customers.

Out of scope: predicting churn within a specific time window, estimating the per-customer effect of an intervention, and scoring customers outside the scoring domain (see Limitations and risks).

## 2. Data

- Source: `{{ data_source }}`, file `{{ data_file }}`. One row per customer, no dates, so there is no temporal validation.
- Input data sha256: `{{ input_data_hash }}` (canonical content after cleaning; recompute with `src.data.load.data_hash`).
- Stratified random split: {{ split.train }} train, {{ split.calib }} calibration, {{ split.test }} test rows. The test set contains {{ n_pos }} churners (base rate {{ "%.3f"|format(base_rate) }}).
- The `tenure` and `TotalCharges` columns are excluded from the features by policy, not because leakage was demonstrated. Using both would raise PR-AUC by {{ "%.3f"|format(ablation.pr_auc.delta) }} on average (diagnostic; see the final report).

