## 7. Limitations and risks

- Evaluation uses a test set of {{ split.test }} rows; the intervals reflect test-set sampling noise only (not training variability or change over time), and differences between models have not been formally tested.
- There is no time axis: performance in future periods is not observed.
- Customers with tenure below the `domain.min_tenure_months` limit in `params.yaml` are flagged `out_of_domain` at prediction time and must not be scored by this model.
- Business value depends on save_rate ({{ "%.2f"|format(save_rate) }}, `{{ save_rate_source }}`); the model does not measure the effect of the intervention.
- The model uses customer attributes only; it has no behavioral or interaction-history features.

